WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Shabbat morning.

2
00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:06.700
A small Jewish community meets to pray,
but there is no rabbi in the room.

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.010
One member, who knows the
prayers, simply leads.

4
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.990
The service goes ahead.

5
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.450
Since the 1800s, Jews have also split
into movements that disagree about how far

6
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.370
Jewish law should change.

7
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.300
So if a service needs no
rabbi, what are rabbis for,

8
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.030
and who else leads?

9
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.290
In this mission, you'll compare Orthodox,

10
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.860
Reform and Liberal Judaism,
from seating to who may lead.

11
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:37.140
Then you'll weigh up a claim: are rabbis
less important today than in the past?

12
00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.130
Your mission: find out
what rabbis are for,

13
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.370
and who else leads Jewish worship.
